# Component Structure

- `src/components/ui/` — Shadcn primitives (Button, Card, Badge, Input, etc.) — do not edit
- `src/components/` — feature components (forms, cards, lists, containers)
- `src/components/settings/`, `billing/`, `dashboard/`, `plans/` — domain-grouped sub-folders

## Naming Convention

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| List container (SWR) | `*-list-container.tsx` | `members-list-container.tsx` |
| Pure list / table | `*-list.tsx` | `members-list.tsx` |
| Card | `*-card.tsx` | `member-card.tsx` |
| Form | `*-form.tsx` | `member-form.tsx` |

# Forms

Use `react-hook-form` + `@hookform/resolvers/zod`. Schemas live in `src/lib/validations/`.

```tsx
const form = useForm<MemberFormValues>({
  resolver: zodResolver(memberFormSchema),
  defaultValues: { ... },
});
```

# Client vs Server Components

- Add `"use client"` only when you need hooks, event handlers, or browser APIs
- Server components fetch directly from Supabase queries — no `fetch()` to own API routes
- Client components fetch data via SWR using the `fetcher` from `@/lib/fetcher`

# Hooks

Custom hooks live in `src/hooks/`:
- `useUser()` — current user, org, trial status (pre-populated from layout via SWR)
- `useTrialGuard(error)` — redirects to billing on 402 response
- `useLocalStorage(key, defaultValue)` — syncs state with localStorage (reads synchronously)
- `useDebounce(value, ms)` — debounce input for search fields
- `usePermissions()` — client-side RBAC checks

# UI Component Imports

Always import Shadcn components from `@/components/ui/*`, not from Radix directly.
